{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VYSBSXJLt99zLjhXR1r82D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment 6 Independent-Examiner Protocol — Session V-E6\n2\t\n3\tYou are **V-E6**, an independent examiner in a fresh, governed session. A\n4\tworker process has produced an answer to the task in `package/task.json`.\n5\tYour job is the `verify-independent` node of the selected topology: re-check\n6\tthat answer against the package with your own derivation. You were not the\n7\tauthor of the answer and hold no write authority over it.\n8\t\n9\tYour session grants only the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not\n10\tattempt to launch any process, session, or agent.\n11\t\n12\t## Workspace layout\n13\t\n14\t```text\n15\tpackage/                     the task package (same materials the worker saw)\n16\tresult.json                  the worker's deliverable (under examination)\n17\tresolution.json              the worker's per-distinction resolution claims\n18\tdistinctions.json            the distinctions the worker was resolving\n19\texaminer-charge.md           (if present) the worker's proposed checking charge\n20\tprotocol.md                  this file\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\t## What you produce\n24\t\n25\t`independent-verification.json`:\n26\t\n27\t```json\n28\t{\n29\t  \"task_id\": \"...\",\n30\t  \"method\": \"how you re-derived/checked, and how it differs from the worker's method\",\n31\t  \"per_distinction\": [\n32\t    {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"verdict\": \"CONCUR|DISSENT|CANNOT_ASSESS\", \"why\": \"...\"}\n33\t  ],\n34\t  \"discrepancies\": [\n35\t    {\"where\": \"result.json field or claim\", \"worker_value\": \"...\",\n36\t     \"examiner_value\": \"...\", \"severity\": \"MATERIAL|MINOR\", \"evidence\": \"...\"}\n37\t  ],\n38\t  \"overall\": \"CONFIRMED|DISPUTED\"\n39\t}\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tGround rules:\n43\t\n44\t- Re-derive; do not merely re-read. Follow `examiner-charge.md` if present,\n45\t  but you are not bound by it: check anything you judge discriminating,\n46\t  especially boundary and edge cases.\n47\t- A discrepancy is MATERIAL if correcting it would change a deliverable\n48\t  field's value.\n49\t- If you find a MATERIAL discrepancy, show the full evidence for your value\n50\t  so a deterministic checker can adjudicate between you and the worker.\n51\t- Honesty over agreement: CONCUR only where your own derivation matches.\n52\t\n53\t## Ledger\n54\t\n55\tMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` (same event schema as every governed\n56\tsession): an `observe` event (actor `examiner`) after reading, a `verify`\n57\tevent (actor `examiner`) referencing `independent-verification.json` when\n58\tyou write it, and a `return` event (actor `examiner`) at the end. No\n59\t`complete` event.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8db6ed65-af74-4f6e-87e3-27fd3f74b3f1","uuid":"ccf2bd31-8dbd-4bbe-acfd-11c93ebd02fb","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:47:58.054Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t08/shadow/examiner-ws/protocol.md","content":"# Experiment 6 Independent-Examiner Protocol — Session V-E6\n\nYou are **V-E6**, an independent examiner in a fresh, governed session. A\nworker process has produced an answer to the task in `package/task.json`.\nYour job is the `verify-independent` node of the selected topology: re-check\nthat answer against the package with your own derivation. You were not the\nauthor of the answer and hold no write authority over it.\n\nYour session grants only the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not\nattempt to launch any process, session, or agent.\n\n## Workspace layout\n\n```text\npackage/                     the task package (same materials the worker saw)\nresult.json                  the worker's deliverable (under examination)\nresolution.json              the worker's per-distinction resolution claims\ndistinctions.json            the distinctions the worker was resolving\nexaminer-charge.md           (if present) the worker's proposed checking charge\nprotocol.md                  this file\n```\n\n## What you produce\n\n`independent-verification.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"...\",\n  \"method\": \"how you re-derived/checked, and how it differs from the worker's method\",\n  \"per_distinction\": [\n    {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"verdict\": \"CONCUR|DISSENT|CANNOT_ASSESS\", \"why\": \"...\"}\n  ],\n  \"discrepancies\": [\n    {\"where\": \"result.json field or claim\", \"worker_value\": \"...\",\n     \"examiner_value\": \"...\", \"severity\": \"MATERIAL|MINOR\", \"evidence\": \"...\"}\n  ],\n  \"overall\": \"CONFIRMED|DISPUTED\"\n}\n```\n\nGround rules:\n\n- Re-derive; do not merely re-read. Follow `examiner-charge.md` if present,\n  but you are not bound by it: check anything you judge discriminating,\n  especially boundary and edge cases.\n- A discrepancy is MATERIAL if correcting it would change a deliverable\n  field's value.\n- If you find a MATERIAL discrepancy, show the full evidence for your value\n  so a deterministic checker can adjudicate between you and the worker.\n- Honesty over agreement: CONCUR only where your own derivation matches.\n\n## Ledger\n\nMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` (same event schema as every governed\nsession): an `observe` event (actor `examiner`) after reading, a `verify`\nevent (actor `examiner`) referencing `independent-verification.json` when\nyou write it, and a `return` event (actor `examiner`) at the end. No\n`complete` event.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
